From fd701699b0f45ae0976343765effa76f466dbe90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: frame-cost <none@invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:49:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_FRAME_COST=1: three log lines every 5 s that split a
 frame's time (present side, GPU thread, textures made again); measurement
 only, off by default

With the switch unset nothing changes: each site is one cached bool check.

- common/frame_cost.h (new): the windows and their lines, standard library only, so it is
  tested off the console (tests/test_frame_cost.cpp).
- nx2_gsv.h PresentClientBuffer: per present, the time the game ran since the last present
  returned, the fence wait, composite and pacing, the frame's fence increments and how many of
  them the GPU thread had not reached when the present came in.
- hitch_trace.h: the operations it already times are also timed with this switch, and their
  totals are logged per 5 s for every frame (EDEN_UP_HITCH_TRACE only logs frames of 100 ms or
  more). No per-operation or per-frame line and no profile zone from this switch.
- texture_cache.h: images made, deleted, and made again at the same address with the same
  format, extent, levels and layers within 3600 frames of a collector's delete.

Not run on a console.
